From: q2q port
Subject: [PATCH] q2q: trace bsd_init steps on SWEET

Enable XNU's DEBUG_BSDINIT step logging (bsd_init_kprintf -> kprintf) on SWEET.
On the Galaxy Z Fold3 the kernel stalls silently inside bsd_init after Mach/IOKit
lockdown; this prints each bsd_init step so the stalling step is visible.

---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
@@ -490,7 +490,11 @@
 	platform_stall_panic_or_spin(PLATFORM_STALL_XNU_LOCATION_BSD_INIT);
 #endif
 
+#if defined(SWEET)
+#define DEBUG_BSDINIT 1 /* q2q: trace bsd_init steps on the console */
+#else
 #define DEBUG_BSDINIT 0
+#endif
 
 #if DEBUG_BSDINIT
 #define bsd_init_kprintf(x, ...) kprintf("bsd_init: " x, ## __VA_ARGS__)
